        "type": "FACT",
        "description": "read_cookie outputs msg[index] via printf(\"%s\", msg[index]) with no length limit",
        "source": "DISASSEMBLY"
      },
      {
        "id": "F014",
        "type": "FACT",
        "description": "GOT is writable (Full RELRO means .got.plt is merged into .got which is in RELRO segment, but .got section at 0x3f58 has WA flags)",
        "source": "ELF"
      },
      {
        "id": "F015",
        "type": "DERIVED",
        "description": "edit_cookie and read_cookie use %llu (unsigned) for index input but jl (signed) for bounds check. A value like 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF is stored as uint64 max but compared as int64 -1, which is < cookie_num, bypassing the check",
        "source": "DISASSEMBLY"
      },
      {
        "id": "F016",
        "type": "DERIVED",
        "description": "msg array (0x4060, 32x8=256 bytes) and msg_size array (0x4160, 32x4=128 bytes) are adjacent in .bss with no gap. msg ends at 0x4160, msg_size starts at 0x4160",
        "source": "ELF"
      },
