    "uncertainties": [
      {
        "id": "U001",
        "description": "Whether the OOB index in edit_cookie can reach a controllable pointer value (e.g., if msg[OOB] reads from msg_size which contains user-controlled values, that value interpreted as a pointer could be written to)",
        "reason": "Depends on exact index value and what global variable is hit. S2 needs to trace the data flow."
      },
      {
        "id": "U002",
        "description": "Whether eat_cookie leaves a dangling pointer that can be exploited (UAF). The swap overwrites msg[random_index] but msg[cookie_num-1] retains the old value if random_index != cookie_num-1",
        "reason": "The freed pointer at msg[cookie_num-1] is at index cookie_num-1 which is now out of the valid range (cookie_num was decremented). edit/read check index < cookie_num, so the dangling slot is not directly accessible without OOB."
      },
      {
        "id": "U003",
        "description": "Whether the OOB read in read_cookie can leak useful addresses (heap, libc, stack) for bypassing ASLR",
        "reason": "Depends on what pointer value exists at the OOB location in .bss/.data. S2 needs to determine what values are stored adjacent to msg."
      },
